 "text": {
  "headline": "US inflation data: US 2-year yield +13 bp, US 10-year yield +12 bp",
  "tone": "Inflation scare session: US 10-year yield and US 2-year yield rose, while US large caps (EB US 100) fell.",
  "lead": [
   "US inflation data dominated the session. News coverage of the theme ran at 3.18x normal, and markets moved the way this kind of news usually moves them, through inflation expectations and rate expectations. US 2-year yield rose 13 bp to 4.86%; US 10-year yield rose 12 bp to 5.10%. Full data on the [[markets|Financial Markets]] page.",
   "In bonds, the US 2-year yield moved +13 bp to 4.86% and the US 10-year yield moved +12 bp to 5.10%. Yields move with expectations for inflation and for the Federal Reserve's next steps; the [[markets|rates table]] has the full curve.",
   "Among havens and currencies, Gold fell 0.5% to $3,868; USD/JPY fell 0.3% to 159.60; EUR/USD fell 0.3% to 1.1014. Gold and the yen tend to gain when investors look for safety, and to slip when risk appetite returns. See [[metals|Hard Assets]] and [[crypto|Crypto & Currencies]].",
   "In risk assets, US large caps (EB US 100) fell 0.6% to 114.69; Bitcoin rose 1.0% to $64,772. The [[outlook|Market Outlook]] puts the wider trend in context."
  ],
  "briefs": {
   "markets": "US 10-year yield rose 12 bp to 5.10%, leaving the gap over the 2-year at +24 bp. The [[markets|Financial Markets]] page has yields, commodities and currencies.",
   "energy": "Brent crude rose 2.2% to $92.14; US natural gas (Henry Hub) rose 3.8% to $3.00. Benchmarks, power prices and supply data on the [[energy|Energy Terminal]].",
   "crypto": "Bitcoin rose 1.0% to $64,772; EUR/USD fell 0.3% to 1.1014. Live rates and a converter on [[crypto|Crypto & Currencies]].",
   "metals": "Gold fell 0.5% to $3,868; Copper fell 0.7% to $13,610/t. Precious and base metals on the [[metals|Hard Assets Terminal]].",
   "estate": "House prices are rising in 61 of the 69 countries we track over the past year; Moldova leads at +33.7%. Country data on the [[estate|Estate Index]].",
   "corporate": "This week's top-ranked bank is East West Bank and the top company is APA Corporation, under a risk-on backdrop. Rankings on the [[corporate|Corporate Monitor]].",
   "outlook": "Our quarterly outlook reads the backdrop as risk-on; Cybersecurity leads the five themes we follow. Full rankings on the [[outlook|Market Outlook]].",
